que
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Curfew's design is que's (https://github.com/queapp-org/que), by the same
author, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0: the layout and every
curfew-* mod draw que's sidebar, tab row, review pane, diff tabs and usage
readout, and themes/curfew.json holds que's palette. Ported from que's code:

- mods/curfew-prs/core.mjs: que's pull request rules (see that folder's NOTICE
  and LICENSE for the files).
- mods/curfew-diff/comments.js and mods/curfew-changes/comments.js: which
  changed lines are only comments, and the language table (que's
  src/daemon/comment-lines.ts and src/daemon/syntax.ts); the comment-line modes
  (Dim, Show, Fold) and their words.
- mods/curfew-usage/usage.mjs: que's usage.decode.ts and usage.ts.
- mods/curfew-claude/statusline.mjs and pr-hook.mjs: que's status line and
  pr-created.ts.
- mods/quiet-hours: que's quiet hours (the board, the logged unlock, quiet now,
  the apply-tonight guardrail, the overnight summary).
- mods/curfew-sidebar/titles.mjs and mods/quiet-hours/names.mjs: que's name for
  a Claude Code session (src/shared/session-label.ts, and capTitle in
  src/shared/brief.ts), which names a sidebar row and a quiet board row.
- mods/curfew-sidebar/workspace.mjs: a new workspace made que's way (the name
  word lists and drawing of src/shared/names.ts; the name clash check, fetch,
  default branch, worktree add and copied includes of src/daemon/workspaces.ts;
  the que.toml and .worktreeinclude rules of src/shared/config.ts), and the
  preparing row (Sidebar.tsx, WorkingMark.tsx). See that folder's NOTICE.
- mods/curfew-project and mods/curfew-sidebar/remove.mjs: Remove project, que's
  way: the project menu's items (Sidebar.tsx), the dialog's words
  (RemoveProjectDialog in src/renderer/src/components/dialogs.tsx), and the
  removal order (WorkspaceManager.removeProject and its removal steps in
  src/daemon/workspaces.ts: the terminals first, then each worktree removed by
  force and pruned, the branches kept). Deleting the worktrees is opt-in here.
- The 16 px line icons are que's (src/renderer/src/components/icons.tsx), or
  drawn in their style for Curfew.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Herdr app's shipped mods
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Parts of these mods are adapted from the mods shipped with the Herdr app
(https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr-app), licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. All of them are modified.

- mods/curfew-changes: adapted from the shipped changes mod (its panel, git
  status handling and commit box). Its changes.svg is the Herdr app's.
- mods/curfew-files: adapted from the shipped files mod (the lazy tree and
  folder listing). Its chevron-down.svg and chevron-right.svg are the Herdr
  app's copies of Lucide icons (licence below).
- mods/curfew-file: the shipped files mod's bounded read-only preview (the read,
  its bounds and words, the language table), moved from curfew-files into a tab.
- mods/curfew-new-session: adapted from the shipped new-menu mod (the menu's
  rows, keys and agent cache).
- mods/curfew-sidebar: the helpers that find where a space is now (base, place,
  where) are adapted from the shipped spaces mod. remove.mjs reads `git worktree
  list --porcelain` and checks for uncommitted changes (git status without
  optional locks or fsmonitor) as the shipped worktree mod does.
- mods/curfew-project: the menu's keys (↑/↓, Enter, Esc) are adapted from the
  shipped menu mod, its rows from the shipped new-menu mod (by way of
  curfew-new-session).
- mods/curfew-tabs, mods/curfew-bar, mods/quiet-hours: the layout-node lookup
  (find) is adapted from the shipped tabs and workspace-chrome mods.
- mods/quiet-hours draws the Herdr app's mods/workspace-chrome/clock.svg, and
  mods/curfew-new-session its icons/shell.svg and
  mods/workspace-chrome/branch.svg, from the person's install; they are not
  copied here.

